What you need to do

1. Install the CLI on agent-01-fsc. Run npm i -g @salesforce/cli, and make sure sf is on the PATH of the runner service account.
2. Check which Windows account runs the runner service. It must be a normal user (not SYSTEM or NETWORK SERVICE) because the CLI stores its login under that user's profile.
3. Log in once as that user. This needs Okta and MFA and finishing within about 2 minutes, with port 1717 free:
sf org login web --alias fsc-qa --instance-url https://htsw--qa.sandbox.my.salesforce.com
sf org list auth
4. Set the GitHub variables. Set BASE_URL, SF_LOGIN_URL and SF_LOGIN_FORM_URL to the same org as the CLI login. Delete or update RUNNER_LABELS if it's already set, and delete AUTH_MODE if it's set to something else.
5. Merge the repo-side items. Merge to main so the schedules start. Optionally make the smoke PR check required in branch protection, and confirm Actions policy and PR-comment permissions.
6. Run gh workflow run scheduled-smoke-regression.yml as a first test.
7. Redo the CLI login if it expires. Repeat the login if the refresh token is revoked or expires. That depends on your org's session policies, which I haven't checked.
